    "chunks": [
      {
        "id": "02-order-service.md#0",
        "heading": "Purpose",
        "characters": 226,
        "embeddedText": "Order Service > Purpose\n\nOrder Service owns the lifecycle of an order after it has been accepted by Core.\nCore remains the system of record for pricing and invoicing; Order Service is\nthe system of record for fulfilment state."
      },
      {
        "id": "02-order-service.md#1",
        "heading": "Order states",
        "characters": 595,
        "embeddedText": "Order Service > Order states\n\nAn order moves through these states, in this order:\n\n1. `received` — created by Core, not yet validated\n2. `validated` — address and stock checks passed\n3. `picking` — assigned to a warehouse\n4. `dispatched` — handed to a carrier, tracking number issued\n5. `delivered` — carrier confirmed delivery\n6. `closed` — invoiced and reconciled\n\nTwo terminal exception states exist: `cancelled` (before dispatch) and\n`returned` (after delivery). An order can never move backwards. Attempting an\ninvalid transition returns HTTP 409 with an error code of `invalid_transition`."
      },
      {
        "id": "02-order-service.md#2",
        "heading": "API",
        "characters": 629,
        "embeddedText": "Order Service > API\n\nThe service exposes a REST API at `https://orders.internal.nordvik.no/v2`.\nAuthentication uses a service token in the `Authorization: Bearer` header;\ntokens are issued by Core and expire after 24 hours.\n\nKey endpoints:\n\n- `GET /orders/{id}` — full order with current state and history\n- `POST /orders/{id}/transition` — request a state change\n- `GET /orders?updated_since=` — incremental sync, max 500 per page\n- `POST /orders/{id}/cancel` — cancels if state is before `dispatched`\n\nThe API is versioned in the path. Version 1 was retired in March 2023 and any\nremaining v1 traffic is rejected with HTTP 410."
      },
      {
        "id": "02-order-service.md#3",
        "heading": "Rate limits and timeouts",
        "characters": 282,
        "embeddedText": "Order Service > Rate limits and timeouts\n\nClients are limited to 600 requests per minute per token. Exceeding this returns\nHTTP 429 with a `Retry-After` header in seconds. The internal HTTP timeout when\nCore calls Order Service is 5 seconds for reads and 15 seconds for transitions."
      },
      {
        "id": "02-order-service.md#4",
        "heading": "Known issues",
        "characters": 400,
        "embeddedText": "Order Service > Known issues\n\nThe `updated_since` cursor uses a timestamp with one second resolution. Orders\nupdated within the same second as the cursor boundary can be returned twice.\nConsumers must therefore be idempotent. This is documented behaviour, not a bug\nthat will be fixed, because changing it would require a table rewrite of\n`order_events`, which currently holds about 400 million rows."
      }
    ]
  },
