      {
        "role": "system",
        "content": "<context>\n[S1] (02-order-service.md > API)\nOrder Service > API\n\nThe service exposes a REST API at `https://orders.internal.nordvik.no/v2`.\nAuthentication uses a service token in the `Authorization: Bearer` header;\ntokens are issued by Core and expire after 24 hours.\n\nKey endpoints:\n\n- `GET /orders/{id}` — full order with current state and history\n- `POST /orders/{id}/transition` — request a state change\n- `GET /orders?updated_since=` — incremental sync, max 500 per page\n- `POST /orders/{id}/cancel` — cancels if state is before `dispatched`\n\nThe API is versioned in the path. Version 1 was retired in March 2023 and any\nremaining v1 traffic is rejected with HTTP 410.\n\n[S2] (06-incident-runbook.md > Orders stuck in `validated`)\nIncident Runbook > Orders stuck in `validated`\n\nAlmost always the warehouse assignment worker has died. Check\n`supervisorctl status order-assign`. If it is stopped, restart it and then\nre-drive the backlog with `php index.php orders reassign --state=validated`.\nIf the worker is running but the backlog is growing, the usual cause is a stock\nservice timeout; check the Order Service logs for `stock_check_timeout`.\n</context>"
      },
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "What authentication does the order API use?"
